      <span
        class="atwp-ba-label atwp-after-label"
      >
        After
      </span>

    </div>

  </div>

</section>


<!-- =========================================================
     DETAILER OR PAINTER
========================================================= -->

<section class="atwp-section">

  <div class="atwp-wrap">


    <div class="atwp-heading atwp-reveal">

      <div class="atwp-kicker">
        Detailer or Painter?
      </div>


      <h2>

        Some paint problems{" "}
        <span class="atwp-gradient">
          need a different shop.
        </span>

      </h2>


      <p>

        Polishing improves the surface.

        It does not replace paint that has already chipped,
        peeled or been damaged too deeply.

      </p>

    </div>


    <div class="atwp-painter-layout">


      <div class="atwp-problem-list atwp-reveal">


        <button
          class="atwp-problem active"

          data-title="Deep scratch"

          data-answer="Polishing may reduce surrounding haze or transfer, but a deep scratch can remain visible. When the damage goes beyond what polishing can improve, paint repair is the better option."

          data-status="Painter / body shop may be needed"

          data-image="/media/blog/can-polishing-remove-scratches/deep_scratch.webp"
        >

          Deep scratch

        </button>


        <button
          class="atwp-problem"

          data-title="Chipped paint"

          data-answer="If paint is missing, polishing cannot put it back. A painter or body shop is the right type of repair."

          data-status="Paint repair"

          data-image="/media/blog/can-polishing-remove-scratches/chipped_paint.webp"
        >

          Chipped paint

        </button>


        <button
          class="atwp-problem"

          data-title="Missing paint"

          data-answer="A polished surface can look cleaner around the damage, but missing paint itself has to be repaired rather than polished."

          data-status="Paint repair"

          data-image="/media/blog/can-polishing-remove-scratches/missing_paint.webp"
        >

          Missing paint

        </button>


        <button
          class="atwp-problem"

          data-title="Clear coat failure"

          data-answer="Once the finish is peeling or failing like this, machine polishing is not the repair. This needs paint work."

          data-status="Painter / body shop"

          data-image="/media/blog/can-polishing-remove-scratches/clear_coat_failure.webp"
        >

          Peeling / clear coat failure

        </button>


      </div>


      <div class="atwp-painter-result atwp-reveal">


        <img
          class="atwp-painter-img"
          id="atwpPainterImage"

          src="/media/blog/can-polishing-remove-scratches/deep_scratch.webp"

          alt="Paint damage example"
        
          loading="lazy"
          decoding="async"
        >


        <div class="atwp-painter-shade"></div>


        <div class="atwp-painter-copy">


          <span
            class="atwp-painter-status"
            id="atwpPainterStatus"
          >
            Painter / body shop may be needed
          </span>


          <h3 id="atwpPainterTitle">
            Deep scratch
          </h3>


          <p id="atwpPainterText">

            Polishing may reduce surrounding haze or transfer,
            but a deep scratch can remain visible.

            When the damage goes beyond what polishing can improve,
            paint repair is the better option.

          </p>


        </div>


      </div>


    </div>

  </div>

</section>


